[h1]Flavorium Universalis v0.3.8 Hotfix[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.3.* BETA | Multiplayer synchronized[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]New: The Concert of Europe[/h2]

The Balance of Power no longer simply ends when the coalition prevails. It becomes an institution. A coalition victory under the right policy founds the [b]Concert of Europe[/b]: a great-power directorate the victors govern, congress by congress.

[list]
[*] [b]A playable directorate:[/b] the strongest victors take seats; the chief balancer becomes founding president, and the chair then [b]rotates by election[/b] (with an on-demand [b]Vote of No Confidence[/b] to unseat a sitting president). New powers are admitted only by a vote of the congress.
[*] [b]Three questions of state, voted in congress:[/b] the [b]guiding Doctrine[/b] (classic Balance of Power, the legitimist Principle of Intervention, or Liberal Internationalism), [b]Collective Security[/b] (ad-hoc concerts or a binding Mutual Guarantee), and whether the powers sit as [b]a Standing Congress[/b].
[*] [b]Collective actions:[/b] with a standing congress the powers may impose [b]Congress Mediation[/b] on a member's wars; they may also mount a [b]Collective Intervention[/b], manage [b]the Eastern Question[/b], and [b]Admit a Power[/b].
[/list]

[h2]New: The Balancing Congress[/h2]

The Balancing Coalition can now convene a parliament of its own and table collective motions, carried by a simple majority of members, drawn from the alliance statecraft of the Napoleonic coalitions:

[list]
[*] [b]Coalition Subsidies[/b] (Pitt's gold): pool a common war-chest in the leader's hands and harden the lesser powers.
[*] [b]Treaty of Chaumont:[/b] a binding pledge of no separate peace that steadies the bloc.
[*] [b]The Pragmatic Army:[/b] a unified command and a real fighting bonus across the coalition.
[*] [b]A Joint Démarche:[/b] a collective ultimatum that swings the contest toward the coalition and sours every member's standing with the aspirant.
[*] [b]The Partition Treaty:[/b] agree the war aims in advance; the prospect of gain steels the bloc for the reckoning.
[/list]

[h2]Reworked: The Reckoning[/h2]

The end-game now resolves along three clear roads, each tracked by its own counter in disjoint share-bands so the races can never fire together. [b]Hegemony[/b] and a [b]Coalition[/b] victory each prime a decisive final war, won on the real treaty rather than a die-roll, while [b]Stagnation[/b] quietly closes a contest that has gone nowhere. A primed reckoning freezes the other roads until its war is settled.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Fixes[/h2]

[list]
[*] Updated the Balance of Power and Invasion of Mexico situations to the patched [b]can_end[/b] syntax (the old [i]end_reason[/i] blocks are no longer read).
[*] Situation map and legend colours moved to named colours, fixing the [i]"badly read script value"[/i] warnings.
[*] Registered the missing Concert/Coalition parliament modifier types and corrected the Concert IO definition, the concert intervention vote scope, and the ending's [b]destroy_international_organization[/b] calls.
[*] Fixed the coalition leader's [b]Subsidise the Allies[/b] option spending no gold (a poisoned accumulator variable).
[/list]
